It occurs to me that an English-Lojban dictionary is needed --- not a full
dictionary, but a list of words and their Lojban equivalents, with the
reader referred off to the gi'uste and jvoste for place structures and
definition details. Such a dictionary would have to be synonym-heavy.

Also, as a preliminary, perhaps, to this, we should take a 'basic' word
list (the Esperanto _Baza Radikaro_ is sitting in my directory with
this in mind), translate it into Lojban, fill in any lexical blanks,
and, uh, stuff like that. I'm not proposing to do this *right* now, 
because...

I'm supposed to be busier than I am: my Pragmatics lecturer wants a draft
